[low] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go:450 (correctness)
The recent_failure_rate check claims to evaluate completed or failed cells from the last 24 hours, but loadRecentCellTotals filters by dashboard_suggestion_runs.started_at. A cell that completes or fails in the last 24 hours on a run started earlier is ignored, so the health check can miss recent failures from long-running or heavily snoozed runs.
Suggested fix: Filter recent cell totals on dashboard_suggestion_run_cells.completed_at >= cutoff with status IN ('completed','failed') instead of the parent run started_at timestamp, and add a regression test for an old run with a newly failed cell.
Guidance: In internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go, fix loadRecentCellTotals so the 24h window is based on dashboard_suggestion_run_cells.completed_at, not dashboard_suggestion_runs.started_at. Remove the join to dashboard_suggestion_runs unless another selected field needs it, add a WHERE clause like `dashboard_suggestion_run_cells.status IN ? AND dashboard_suggestion_run_cells.completed_at >= ?` with []string{"completed", "failed"} and time.Now().UTC().Add(-24*time.Hour), and keep the SELECT counting completed vs failed statuses. Be careful not to count pending cells with NULL completed_at. Add a regression test in internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestions_integration_test.go that creates a run started more than 24h ago, creates a failed cell with completed_at inside the last 24h, calls the summary endpoint, and asserts the recent_failure_rate check reflects that failed recent cell instead of passing because the parent run is old.

