- [medium] internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker.go:106 (correctness): The rate-limit snooze budget is checked with job.Attempt, but River v0.30 explicitly does not count snoozes as attempts and the executor decrements the attempt when JobSnooze is returned. Under a persistent 429, job.Attempt never reaches maxRateLimitSnoozes, so the cell can snooze indefinitely instead of eventually failing and finalizing the run as the code comment intends.
- [low] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go:791 (correctness): rateLimitPressureCheck returns pass with the message "No dashboard suggestion rate-limit snoozes were observed" whenever there are zero completed/failed cells, even if RateLimitedTotal is non-zero from pending cells. A newly throttled run with only pending cells and five snoozes will therefore report a passing rate_limit_pressure check while the totals already show throttling.
